From 8319b8661f1e46730ad9ba76d69bdc730ddb475e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:00:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(status): local card identity uses the board-root
 owner profile, never the reader's

Transport ruling C9/F10: kanban_home() is shared across profiles, so the
active profile gave one card different identity_keys in different consumers.
Cards now carry the hub collect_qualified_tasks rule: <root> -> default,
<root>/profiles/P -> P; a board outside the root has no guessed profile and
stays unknown. Applied to the list, sidebar-count (incl. done receipts) and
card-detail entry paths. Processes/subagents keep their session profile.

Proof: test_kanban_card_owner_profile.py RED 5 failed on the old scope,
GREEN 11/11; fixtures whose board sits under the root now say so via
HERMES_HOME. 28 related files 773 passed.
